General. These provisions shall apply to petitions for variances filed with the city.
Criteria for issuance. No petition for variance shall be granted unless the petitioner affirmatively demonstrates that one (1) or more of the following
circumstances exists:
The variance is essential to protect public health or safety;
Compliance with this section will require measures which, because their extent or cost impose undue hardship, cannot be accomplished within
the anticipated duration of the shortage or will not ensure equitable distribution;
Alternative restrictions, which achieve the same level of demand reduction as the restrictions from which a variance is sought, are available and
are binding and enforceable.
Petitions for variance. The petition shall contain the following:
The petitioner's name, address and telephone number;
The specific section of the Code, ordinance, rules or regulations from which the petitioner is requesting relief;
A detailed statement of the facts which the petitioner believes demonstrates that the request qualifies for a variance, which may include reports
by qualified technical experts;
A description of the relief desired;
The period of time for which the variance is sought, including the reasons and facts in support thereof;
The damage or harm resulting or which may result to petitioner from compliance with the Code, ordinance, rules or regulations;
